  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Pre-oxidizing polished AlNbTaTiZr at 1000–1100 °C in 0.1 atm O2 for 10–20 hours will form a continuous Al2O3 surface scale.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pre-formed Al2O3 scale will be uniform and adherent.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pre-formed Al2O3 scale will be nanocrystalline.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled pre-oxidation promotes preferential oxidation of Al in the alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al can form an external oxide when its outward diffusive flux is sufficiently large relative to the inward oxygen flux.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Al2O3 scale is slow-growing and has low oxygen permeability.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A continuous Al2O3 scale will act as a barrier to oxygen ingress.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::web::009::discussion",
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxygen barrier will limit further oxidation of the refractory HEA substrate during prolonged high-temperature exposure.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::web::009::discussion",
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Discontinuous Al2O3 does not provide an effective oxidation barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::web::009::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pre-oxidation will improve the high-temperature oxygen resistance of AlNbTaTiZr relative to the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::web::009::discussion",
        "PMC6804173::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 100 hours in pure oxygen at 1000 °C, pre-oxidized specimens will have significantly lower weight gain than untreated specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the service exposure, pre-oxidized specimens will exhibit less oxide-scale thickening than untreated specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the service exposure, pre-oxidized specimens will retain a more coherent and intact oxide layer than untreated specimens.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated AlNbTaTiZr exposed directly to pure oxygen at 1000 °C typically undergoes rapid, uncontrolled oxide growth and high weight gain.",
      "field": "baseline",
